      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The GDPR is quite strict about this, and you must treat it as a high-priority task, not just a quick sweep of the main database. You are obligated to take \"reasonable steps\" to ensure the data is erased from all systems, which includes backups and secondary logs. If you can't find it, you must demonstrate that you have made a diligent effort to search for it, which is a key part of proving compliance. It's an ongoing, diligent process, not a one-time cleanup.",
      "source": "target",
